    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0588" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.6363/34</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Liaison Officer</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Alling</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-29">April 29, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Alling</hi>: At the meeting of the Liaison
                        Committee<anchor n="33" xml:id="d687-f1"/> held on Monday, April 27, the
                    protection of the oil installations in Saudi Arabia was considered. The
                    representative of the War Department <pb facs="0589" n="577" xml:id="pg577"/>
                    stated that that Department had at present no plans to send any forces or
                    equipment to the region in question. It is the belief that while a possibility
                    of an air raid on the oil fields of that region exists the danger to the
                    refineries on Bahrein Island is much greater.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Orme Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d687-f1" n="33" xml:id="d687-f1-content">
                <p>Composed of the Chief of Staff, Chief of Naval Operations, and the Under
                    Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
